      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first telegraph line in Ridgeway ran in 1855, with wires stretched from tree to tree, and it played a key role during the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofridgeway.com/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Virginia State historic marker on Route 220 commemorates William Byrd II’s 1728 survey party that crossed the Ridgeway area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
